r token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-04-19","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"faces":[],"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{G}","name":"Runeclaw Bear","oracle_id":"ec49dfcf-d16d-4621-af4b-4a6f09043221","oracle_text":"","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2014-07-18","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Bear"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect modifies how many +1/+1 counters you put on Nantuko Cultivator, the number of cards you draw isn't modified. Likewise, if an effect modifies how many cards you draw, the number of +1/+1 counters you put on Nantuko Cultivator won't be modified.","oracle_id":"b8dab16c-681c-4abe-b164-fcfb5dc66678","published_at":"2019-06-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You discard, put counters, and draw all while Nantuko Cultivator's ability is resolving. Nothing can happen between the three, and no player may choose to take actions.","oracle_id":"b8dab16c-681c-4abe-b164-fcfb5dc66678","published_at":"2019-06-14","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
